{"lines":[{"t":"1718867188","w":0.069958845774332645,"x":0.7716049391467531,"c":0.5,"h":0.008720930389296444,"y":0.046511627815394085},{"t":"GEMMA:","w":0.053497943878173831,"x":0.10288065801976082,"y":0.098837209417569905,"c":1,"h":0.0087209298276508251},{"t":"ED:","w":0.026748971939086902,"h":0.011627907185728592,"x":0.1008230450232549,"c":1,"y":0.12645348812225199},{"x":0.1028177345870588,"c":1,"t":"GEMMA:","h":0.0091146041142224909,"y":0.14079153506256104,"w":0.053623790740966806},{"x":0.19334804828740534,"w":0.58655990600585939,"c":1,"t":"Yeah, and they can also be understood on different levels. The characters have","y":0.094966531451295189,"h":0.015669454253323667},{"h":0.012011304480167406,"w":0.088576730092366524,"t":"such depth.","x":0.19336595586880909,"y":0.11172690587491085,"c":1},{"y":0.125000000263355,"x":0.1934156610586994,"c":1,"h":0.011631330977620702,"w":0.48559666951497399,"t":"Right - which allows directors to experiment and find new angles."},{"x":0.19319096564003108,"h":0.015281901904354411,"c":1,"w":0.25556355794270841,"t":"That's really important because …..","y":0.13915053157826862},{"t":"Q30","h":0.013081394460653373,"c":1,"x":0.81893004156567595,"w":0.034979422887166378,"y":0.095930232838714047},{"t":"PART 4","y":0.18582967806816464,"h":0.014968550808999725,"x":0.10076001129751798,"c":1,"w":0.098891499837239563},{"t":"Right, everyone, let's make a start. Over the past few sessions, we've been considering the","x":0.10288064820542313,"y":0.21220930220197143,"c":1,"w":0.67695475260416671,"h":0.013081395583944722},{"c":1,"w":0.68323094685872399,"t":"reasons why some world languages are in decline, and today I'm going to introduce another","x":0.10077959565807362,"h":0.015118640499766522,"y":0.22633168702291417},{"t":"factor that affects languages, and the speakers of those languages, and that's technology","c":1,"y":0.24116607755967723,"x":0.10082307018312871,"h":0.013250883392226132,"w":0.66460901896158853},{"x":0.10288064921866161,"y":0.25581395336836876,"t":"and, in particular, digital technology. In order to illustrate its effect, I'm going to focus on the","h":0.013081395583944611,"c":1,"w":0.67078191121419273},{"t":"Icelandic language, which is spoken by around 321,000 people, most of whom live in Iceland","y":0.27031802128592264,"w":0.68518519083658846,"h":0.011778563015312216,"c":1,"x":0.10288065563133339},{"t":"- an island in the North Atlantic Ocean.","x":0.1028056779862915,"y":0.28361081388633447,"w":0.29237378438313799,"h":0.01294324984960471,"c":1},{"h":0.011629619081674702,"c":1,"x":0.10288065205165803,"t":"The problem for this language is not the number of speakers - even though this number","w":0.65226338704427089,"y":0.30668604640524799},{"w":0.62962961832682296,"h":0.013081395583944833,"x":0.10288066399366594,"t":"is small. Nor is it about losing words to other languages, such as English. In fact, the.","y":0.32122093011253616,"c":1},{"h":0.013250883392226132,"c":1,"y":0.33568904596040205,"t":"vocabulary of Icelandic is continually increasing because when speakers need a new word","w":0.67283950805664072,"x":0.098765431059977302},{"h":0.01453488398216074,"w":0.68518519083658846,"x":0.098765429379790437,"t":"for something, they tend to create one, rather than borrowing from another language. All this","y":0.34883720916491834,"c":1},{"t":"makes Icelandic quite a special language - it's changed very little in the past millennium,","w":0.65647008260091155,"y":0.36284309386183655,"h":0.014439066110707555,"c":1,"x":0.10282682278104943},{"t":"yet it can handle twenty-first-century concepts related to the use of computers and digital","h":0.014723203769140158,"w":0.66255142211914064,"c":1,"x":0.09876544138996915,"y":0.37779740852462351},{"x":0.10082304517689324,"y":0.39244186034512207,"w":0.66666666666666663,"h":0.013081395583944611,"c":1,"t":"technology. Take, for example, the word for web browser ... this is vafri in Icelandic, which"},{"x":0.10288066116697668,"w":0.64814814249674479,"c":1,"y":0.40694935205944049,"t":"comes from the verb 'to wander'. I can't think of a more appropriate term because that's","h":0.011778563015311994},{"t":"exactly what you do mentally when you browse the internet. Then there's an Icelandic word","x":0.1028806655598809,"y":0.42137809205377752,"h":0.011778563015312105,"w":0.67489710489908861,"c":1},{"c":1,"y":0.43604651151973517,"t":"for podcast - which is too hard to pronounce! And so on.","x":0.10288065785977844,"w":0.41975308736165368,"h":0.011627907185728592},{"x":0.10082305616082256,"h":0.014534883982160851,"y":0.45784883707620661,"w":0.65020573933919268,"c":1,"t":"Icelandic, then, is alive and growing, but - and it's a big but - young Icelanders spend a"},{"h":0.014723203769140158,"t":"great deal of time in the digital world and this world is predominantly English. Think about","c":1,"y":0.47084805678359942,"x":0.10082305791162298,"w":0.66255142211914064},{"c":1,"h":0.011627907185728592,"x":0.10082304140028327,"w":0.69135803222656245,"t":"smartphones. They didn't even exist until comparatively recently, but today young people use","y":0.48691860454481906},{"h":0.013081395583944722,"c":1,"t":"them all the time to read books, watch TV or films, play games, listen to music, and so on.","x":0.10288065838646948,"y":0.49999999987525867,"w":0.66666666666666674},{"y":0.51438571800335486,"h":0.013894683199861091,"c":1,"x":0.1028466149659702,"t":"Obviously, this is a good thing in many respects because it promotes their bilingual skills, but","w":0.68732014973958333},{"w":0.67695475260416671,"x":0.10082303516307244,"t":"the extent of the influence of English in the virtual world is staggering and it's all happening.","h":0.013081395583944722,"y":0.52906976732123601,"c":1},{"h":0.011751650078979048,"c":1,"t":"really tast.","w":0.07822599411010743,"y":0.54499626796730394,"x":0.10080469832408255},{"h":0.013250883392226243,"c":1,"t":"For their parents and grandparents, the change is less concerning because they already","y":0.56537102456309274,"w":0.65226338704427089,"x":0.10288065205268149},{"x":0.10288069234038062,"t":"have their native-speaker skills in Icelandic. But for young speakers - well, the outcome is a","c":1,"w":0.67901229858398438,"h":0.013089955063675052,"y":0.57848837231909189},{"c":1,"h":0.01453488398216074,"t":"little troubling. For example, teachers have found that playground conversations in Icelandic","x":0.10082303417355329,"y":0.59447674405319506,"w":0.68312759399414058},{"w":0.66049382527669265,"c":1,"h":0.013250883392226132,"x":0.1008230461124585,"y":0.60895170805921239,"t":"secondary schools can be conducted entirely in English, while teachers of much younger"},{"y":0.62142348728020003,"h":0.015547332269423619,"x":0.10076729038731126,"t":"children have reported situations where their classes find it easier to say what is in a picture","c":1,"w":0.679122060139974},{"w":0.69341562906901044,"c":1,"h":0.011627906062437354,"t":"using English, rather than Icelandic. The very real and worrying consequence of all this is that","y":0.63662790724009932,"x":0.10288065285232638},{"y":0.65253239100670513,"c":1,"h":0.011778563015312105,"t":"the young generation in Iceland is at risk of losing its mother tongue.","x":0.10288066555244531,"w":0.50823043823242187},{"x":0.81687242859313569,"y":0.32122093009386621,"h":0.011627907185728592,"c":1,"t":"Q32","w":0.037037035624186143},{"t":"Q33","w":0.034979422887166378,"c":1,"y":0.42005813934465552,"h":0.013081395583944722,"x":0.8189300416085431},{"t":"Q34","w":0.034979422887166267,"h":0.013081395583944722,"c":1,"x":0.81893004161197236,"y":0.47093023237517884},{"w":0.034979422887166378,"h":0.013081395583944722,"t":"Q35","c":1,"x":0.81893004155367333,"y":0.51453488355977184},{"c":1,"t":"Q36","y":0.59447674404735451,"h":0.011627907185728592,"w":0.034979422887166378,"x":0.81893004153995586},{"h":0.013081395583944722,"y":0.62209302306558578,"c":1,"t":"Q37","w":0.034979422887166378,"x":0.8189300416085431},{"c":1,"x":0.10288065644696009,"y":0.69316843321374033,"w":0.67901234944661459,"t":"Of course, this is happening to other European languages too, but while internet companies","h":0.014723203769140158},{"x":0.10288065393498835,"t":"might be willing to offer, say, French options in their systems, it's much harder for them","w":0.63991770426432282,"h":0.013081395583944722,"c":1,"y":0.7078488370895164},{"x":0.10288066932912453,"h":0.011778563015312105,"w":0.65020573933919268,"t":"to justify the expense of doing the same for a language that has a population the size of","y":0.72232037674225247,"c":1},{"c":1,"x":0.10288066210024031,"t":"a French town, such as Nice. The other drawback of Icelandic is the grammar, which is","y":0.73691860454470648,"w":0.64197530110677092,"h":0.011627907185728592},{"t":"significantly more complex than in most languages. At the moment, the tech giants are simply","x":0.10284343932101621,"y":0.75022329979869795,"h":0.012879972042267984,"w":0.69349517822265616,"c":1},{"x":0.10082304124116651,"t":"not interested in tackling this.","y":0.76590106023401139,"c":1,"h":0.011778563015312105,"w":0.22016461690266928},{"h":0.011778563015312105,"c":1,"w":0.68106994628906248,"t":"So, what is the Icelandic government doing about this? Well, large sums of money are being","x":0.10288066461012221,"y":0.78769140142515282},{"h":0.013081395583944722,"t":"allocated to a language technology fund that it is hoped will lead to the development of","w":0.64197530110677092,"y":0.8008720929033909,"c":1,"x":0.10288066211147807},{"h":0.013250883392226132,"x":0.10288064640398792,"t":"Icelandic sourced apps and other social media and digital systems, but clearly this is going to","y":0.81537102456296517,"w":0.68930043538411456,"c":1},{"t":"be an uphill struggle.","x":0.10288066204301999,"w":0.15637859344482419,"y":0.82979976445613746,"h":0.011778563015312105,"c":1},{"c":1,"x":0.81893004158110827,"t":"Q38","w":0.034979422887166267,"y":0.73546511603070208,"h":0.013081395583944611},{"t":"105","x":0.84773662595821253,"y":0.86773255796252025,"w":0.034979422887166378,"c":1,"h":0.013081395583944722},{"y":0.95314993691982619,"w":0.30619837443033859,"c":1,"x":0.66984496081179823,"h":0.035152653221247165,"t":"IELTSXpress.com"}],"h":3395,"w":2400}